{
  "layerSetId": "eskara-2026",
  "campus": "nsc",
  "timeBase": "relative",
  "_readme": [
    "VERIFICATION DATASET, not 2026 content. Every name below is the real 2025 ESKARA",
    "line-up, recovered from 26eskara/archive/notion/2025-eskara and from the note_ko",
    "column of eskara-2026-places.csv, mapped onto the 62 surveyed plots. The 2026",
    "line-up is not authored yet; when it arrives it replaces this file wholesale and",
    "the importer is unchanged.",
    "",
    "timeBase is \"relative\": every offset is minutes from the moment the importer",
    "runs, and days:[1,2] shifts the second document 24h on. That is deliberate — it",
    "puts closed, open, upcoming and unknown on the map at once and crosses several",
    "status boundaries within about ten minutes of importing, which is what makes the",
    "client-side clock recomputation observable. Real content will use",
    "timeBase:\"absolute\" with ISO instants.",
    "",
    "Deliberate coverage, so a reader knows these are not mistakes:",
    "  - daybooth-02 and daybooth-04 each carry TWO occupants, because the 2025",
    "    부스전 sheet numbered two booths 2 and two booths 4. That exercises the",
    "    stackKey merge on a shared plot.",
    "  - truck-05 is lifecycle:\"cancelled\" with a window spanning now, so only the",
    "    lifecycle makes it closed. It must render visibly cancelled, never absent.",
    "  - daybooth-09 is \"draft\" and promo-02 is \"hidden\". Neither may materialize.",
    "  - main-stage has startAt but no endAt, which is the one-sided window that",
    "    materializes as status \"unknown\".",
    "  - the four toilets, 의무실, 배리어프리존 and the selfie booth carry no window",
    "    at all — always-on, and the second case §9 tells the client not to recompute."
  ],

